  ('E.6', 'Known', 'The standard profinite GT braid action is a↦a^lambda, b↦f(a²,b²)^-1 b^lambda f(a²,b²), with z↦z^lambda.', ['C4 §53 announced SN1,1 construction, scans 222–227'], ['Nakamura2013Eisenstein, (5.4.2)','DolgushevLeLorenz2024, §2 and Appendix A','E.2'], False, 'Primary formulas and operadic coherence opened; inverse GT element proves invertibility. This is the standard braid base point.'),
  ('E.7', 'Proved', 'For actual peripheral-line-preserving automorphisms of the profinite free group of rank two, the normalizer of Bhat3 is a split extension of GT-hat by Bhat3.', ['C4 §53, scans 222–227; normalizer comparison with LM3 E.10'], ['E.2','E.6','Asada2001, §1.3 Lemma 1 and §7 Theorem 5','MinamideNakamura2022, Proposition 3.2(iii) and Theorem 4.3','HaranJardenPop2002, Proposition 4.4'], False, 'Peripheral centralizer and normalizer proved; Ferrari sequence and characteristic kernel verified; strict fixing of c instead gives GT1. Based normalizer is not confused with the outer quotient.'),
  ('E.8', 'Known', 'The Tate–Weierstrass arithmetic section has the Kummer correction a^-8rho2 on the second braid generator; its quotient is G_Q, not asserted equal to GT-hat.', ['C4 §53 announced arithmetic SN1,1 construction'], ['E.6','E.7','Nakamura2013Eisenstein, (5.7.1), (5.7.2), Proposition 5.7.3'], False, 'Full based correction is a^-8rho2 z^4rho2. The half-twist change of free basis aligns Nakamura tau1,tau2 with the A,B convention used in Part D.'),
- ('E.9', 'Proved', 'All charming GT-shadows in the pure-abelian compatible braid quotients with |Q3(m)|≤1000 are listed and genuine; separate congruence matrix candidates are audited without being called shadows.', ['C4 §53 action formulas; prompt E(d) computational request'], ['E.6','E.8','DolgushevLeLorenz2024, Theorem B.2'], False, 'Executed m=1,…,5, giving 13 genuine shadows; all cyclic quotients through order 1000 and 304192 power automorphisms checked. Matrix moduli 2,…,10 yield the stated candidate/descent counts. Not an enumeration of all finite quotients under the bound.'),
