  ('E.10', 'Proved', 'Covering germs of a punctured surface are Z-sets, their finite part is finite continuous Zhat-sets, and tangent rays give the stated geometric and profinite transport torsors.', ['C4 scans 241–272, §53.5'], [], False, 'Explicit polar universal-cover construction proves arbitrary-cover descent for this cofinal disk system; no uniform descent theorem for arbitrary spaces is assumed. Smooth-divisor and normal-crossing local models also proved.'),
  ('E.11', 'Refuted', 'The literal inverse 2-limit of the full small topoi of shrinking punctured disks is degenerate; the covering-germ topos is instead BZ.', ['C4 scans 242–243, fols. 768′–769, parenthetical topos proposal'], ['E.10'], False, 'A cone forces every exterior annulus to pull back to zero although their union is terminal. Explicit small-site replacement and pro-topos alternative given. Manuscript good-case qualification retained.'),
  ('E.12', 'Known', 'For hyperbolic marked compact surfaces the differential and topological lifted actions have the same special component extension; the low-type exceptions have smaller or absent tangent kernels.', ['C4 scans 222–227 and 273–280, particularly scan 277'], ['E.10','EarleEells1967, Theorem 1','Hamstrom1974, Theorems 1.5.1–1.5.2 and §1.7','Palais1966, Theorems 5 and 15','Hatcher2022Torus, Theorem B and Handle Smoothing Theorem','Epstein1966, Theorem 3.1 and Appendix A1–A4'], False, 'Primary theorem texts opened. Weak contractibility suffices on Homeo; Frechet ANR argument gives actual contractibility on Diff. Explicit derivative homotopy and (0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(1,0) calculations. Component comparison is justified separately by smoothing and cut-graph isotopies.'),
